-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107, after review: a deadline that reads a section GIVEN
-- is not worked out. `the deal` supplies `the period` with WITH, so its run's
-- deadline is 20; worked out in the module, the GIVEN reads its TYPICALLY
-- default, and the deadline comes out 30. `anchored deal` is the same through
-- an OF anchor (20 in the run, 35 worked out), which l4 explore on unstable
-- works out so. `the plain deal` supplies nothing, so 30 is its run's
-- answer too; it is not worked out either.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the deal` MEANS `the duty` WITH `the period` IS 10 PLUS 10

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the plain deal` MEANS `the duty`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`anchored deal` MEANS `the anchored duty` WITH `the start` IS 10 PLUS 5

§ `Terms`
    GIVEN `the period` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `the period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

§ `Anchored terms`
    GIVEN `the start` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the anchored duty` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 5 OF `the start` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
